    "turn_text": "Knowing your limits is always the best bet. Oh, before we start, just a reminder, this week, Thursday, from 6 to 8 p.m. at Olive Tree and Vine, our latest sponsor to the Allen Sanders Show, Americans for Prosperity, will be sponsoring a jingle and mingle. That's 26 West Main Street in Cartersville from 6 to 8 p.m. Olive Tree and Vine. Just put that in your maps and your GPS and say, Olive Tree and Vine, Cartersville, Georgia, and come join us from 6 to 8 p.m. That's tomorrow, if you're listening on the day this releases, Thursday, come on out. It's going to be a festive evening lined up. Enjoy a live Christmas singer, delicious food, and drinks all on AFP. It's a perfect way to kick off the season all while learning about the ways you can get involved with Americans for prosperity. From days at the Capitol to other educational events, you can discover how you can be a part of making lasting change that will protect the American dream. So come out, have a great time, and then find out how you can make a real impact in your community and beyond. Can't wait to see you there Thursday, Olive Tree and Vine from 6 to 8 p.m. Downtown Cartersville. Hey everyone, welcome back to another episode of The Alan Sander Show, a special bonus episode, and it's my pleasure to welcome once again, not only my Congressman representing me in Northwest Georgia, but the chair of the House Subcommittee looking into not only what happened, the failures of January 6, but then potential weaponization or politicization of the original J6 Committee. Welcome to the show, Congressman Barry Loudermilk.",
