    "turn_text": "Alright, let's start from the beginning today and it was great to get the report as it was dropped. I had my copy given to me so I could use it for my show today. Let's talk a little bit about what I've been chatting about for the last several days. We initially heard from the former chair of the J6, Benny Thompson, saying, I don't need a pardon. We did everything right. Two days later, well, You know, if one was out there, you know, we'd probably consider it to now, oh, yeah, if one's offered, I'm going to suggest we all take it. I have to imagine there's some pressure knowing this interim report specifically says these guys hit exculpatory evidence destroyed or somehow misplaced the documents and the testimony and the stuff that they're supposed to keep forever. So what's happening and is there a reason why Benny Thompson would change his tune wanting a pardon?",
