    "turn_text": "Right. So we went back to the inspector general's office and, and to your point, um, these are things that we knew, in fact, I knew for a fact from early on in 2023 that general millie had identified that Donald Trump told him on January 3rd to deploy the National Guard. The problem was, those were in classified documents. And so I could not release those, right? And so we tried to get those documents classified. That's the executive branch and the Biden administration wasn't going to touch that. What the reason we were able to release it is because in the investigation into Department of Defense, we were able to get General Milley's transcribed interview or his deposition to the IG where he admitted that in an unclassified setting. So we were able to bring that together. Now, a lot of us knew a lot of this information, but you didn't have the hard, solid evidence. That's what this gave us is, look, The media can't even ignore it at this point. We have their words under oath saying exactly what Donald Trump has said from the beginning. We also now know because we have released the HBO film that Nancy Pelosi actually took responsibility initially. So going back to your question on the Inspector General. So we went and we are currently going back and forth with the Inspector General of the Department of Defense saying you need to correct your report. came back and said, well, we don't correct reports. How could you not correct a report when everything in your investigation points to a purposeful delay of the National Guard, but you blame the National Guard?",
