    "turn_text": "right? That is some critical information that needs to be dealt into deeper. You know, some people are saying, okay, we know now they had assets on the ground. We've known they've had assets on the ground for a long time. You expect that. Whenever there's large gatherings here, there are undercover officers from FBI, DEA, part police embedded in the crowds for safety, right? What the Inspector General is reporting is that there were these human resources that they have, you know, confidential human resources. These are informants that are embedded deep within the extremist organizations. That's who these were. They were spies. There were people who are members of Proud Boys or Oath Keepers that are paid undercover by the FBI to inform them. And in fact, some of these we understand were in the higher etchilons of leadership within these organizations. So that's what this is reporting is that they were these paid informants who were here that day. We also have an intelligence report from the Norfolk Office of FBI, it's been known as the Norfolk Report, that was sent days before January 6 that they had intercepted intelligence by extremist groups that there was a planned attack on the Capitol for January 6, okay? So that's a separate report that comes in. So if you've got all of these confidential human resources that are coming here, what had they reported to you beforehand? What information did the FBI have about a potential attack on the Capitol and when did they know it and more importantly, what did they do with it?",
